ents_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crisbeto/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/crisbeto/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Which @angular/* package(s) are the source of the bug?\r\n\r\ncommon\r\n\r\n### Is this a regression?\r\n\r\nNo\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\n```html\r\n<div \r\n  [class]=\"['as-array', 'as-array2']\" \r\n  [class.specific]=\"true\"\r\n></div>\r\n// Applied: All classes are applied\r\n\r\n<div\r\n  [class]=\"['as-array', '', 'as-array2']\" \r\n  [class.specific]=\"true\"\r\n></div>\r\n// Applied: .specific\r\n\r\n<div \r\n  [class]=\"['as-array', false, 'as-array2']\" \r\n  [class.specific]=\"true\"\r\n></div>\r\n// Applied: .as-array .false .as-array2 .specific\r\n\r\n<div \r\n  [class]=\"['as-array', undefined, 'as-array2']\" \r\n  [class.specific]=\"true\"\r\n></div>\r\n// Applied: .as-array\r\n\r\n<div \r\n  [class]=\"['as-array', null, 'as-array2']\" \r\n  [class.specific]=\"true\"\r\n></div>\r\n// Applied: No classes were applied.\r\n```\r\n\r\nMy expectation is basically that falsy values in an array will not be printed and will not affect other class declarations.\r\nBasically I always expect to get `.as-array .as-array2 .specific`.\r\n\r\nI cannot find logic in how it current works. There are 4 different behaviours based on what falsy value is used.\r\nThis can lead to unexpected behaviour and hard to diagnose errors.\r\n\r\n### Please provide a link to a minimal reproduction of the bug\r\n\r\nhttps://stackblitz.com/edit/angular-ivy-amqsbq?file=src/app/app.component.htmlpp%2Fapp.component.html\r\n\r\n### Please provide the exception or error you saw\r\n\r\n_No response_\r\n\r\n### Please provide the environment you discovered this bug in (run `ng version`)\r\n\r\n```true\r\nAngular 15.0.2\r\nNode v16.16.0\r\n```\r\n\r\n\r\n### Anything else?\r\n\r\n_No response_","closed_by":{"login":"angular-robot[bot]","id":56403804,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NTY0MDM4MDQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/43341?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/angular-robot%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/angular-robot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angular-robot%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angular-robot%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angular-robot%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angular-robot%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angular-robot%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angular-robot%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angular-robot%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angular-robot%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/angular-robot%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/48473/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/angular/angular/issues/48473/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed","pinned_comment":null}